section(1,'Final Status','**FINAL STATUS: FAIL**\n\nThe cleanup preserves the bank, resolves its demonstrated economic calculations, and produces faithful exports. It does not yet satisfy the requested pedagogical acceptance criteria. Exact remaining defects are documented below; none was repaired during verification.')
section(2,'Executive Summary',f"All 2,123 claimed changes exist exactly as recorded. No shared General/Micro record drift, revised-key ambiguity, arithmetic mismatch, build failure or export mismatch was found. Verification identified **{len(bycat['F'])} weak checkpoints, {len(bycat['G'])} repair/bridge failures, {len(bycat['D'])} difficulty mismatches and {len(bycat['C'])} metadata/skill defects**. These produce {len(exceptions)} exceptions across {counts['affectedExceptionIDs']} unique IDs.\n\n"+table(['Check','Result','Count / Detail','Blocking?'],summary)+'\n\nScope is the canonical Composer library only. Polished-game banks were neither imported nor edited. This is verification of the original exact scope, not a new bank-wide editorial audit. The companion JSON includes every finding disposition and question-level review ledger.')
section(3,'Bank Integrity',f"Current projection: Global 9,779; General 1,589; Micro 6,301; Macro 4,745. Macro membership exactly matches the pre-cleanup projection. No additions/deletions, empty stems, empty feedback, non-distinct four-option sets, unresolved answer hashes, conflicting aliases, invalid registered image references or parse failures. Structural metadata and pool references pass the active contracts; semantic metadata exceptions are separate.\n\nBaseline commit: `{A['headAtAudit']}`. Baseline source SHA-256: `{A['canonicalSHA256']}`. Verification before/after source SHA-256: `{S['sourceSHA256']}`.")
section(4,'Cleanup Ledger Reconciliation',f"Compared every intended final field and removed field with current canonical values, reconstructed each final record from the baseline, checked unrecorded field changes and all placements. **2,123 VERIFIED CURRENT; 0 REGRESSED / LOST; 0 SUPERSEDED; 0 CANNOT VERIFY.** The affected union is exactly 2,179.\n\nAll 56 retained records and placements are unchanged, but only {counts['retainedLegitimate']} no-change dispositions are pedagogically justified. The other four retained IDs are ECON-NL-HARD-249, ECON-NL-HARD-270, LG-Q-200 and LG-Q-259; their final tasks remain routine despite Hard labels. Exact intended-state reconciliation is not proof that the intended state closes the finding.")
section(5,'134 Finding Closure Verification',f"{passed} findings are verified closed/adjudicated; {failed} retain a defect. Overlapping findings were evaluated against one current state; successful option changes do not automatically close a separate metadata or checkpoint finding. No cannot-verify disposition remains.\n\n"+table(['Finding','Class','Targets','Outcome','Remaining exact IDs'],[(x['findingID'],x['category'],len(x['affectedQuestionIDs']),x['outcome'],', '.join(x['remainingIDs']) or '—') for x in closure]))
section(6,'Instructor-Adjudicated Cases',"MAA-0032: LG-Q-9 and LG-Q-2004 accurately use the ample-reserves framework, distinguish the target range from administered-rate implementation, and do not make routine bond trading the primary current mechanism. Historical/scarce-reserves items retain their stated model. The interpretation is consistent with the Federal Reserve's [ample-reserves implementation explanation](https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/implementing-monetary-policy-in-an-ample-reserves-regime-the-basics-note-1-of-3-20200701.html).\n\nMAA-0093: PM2D2-MULT-L-001 yields A=60/(1−.8)−100=200 and B=60/(1−.6)−20=130, difference 70. PM2D2-MULT-L-002: 80/(1−.75)=320; net 230 implies total offset 90. ECON-SP-HARD-230: 80/(1−.75)−100=220. All describe the offset as total AD reduction after induced effects and subtract it once; feedback agrees.\n\nMAA-0111: ECON-SP-EASYBOSS-2002 uses currency 900 + checking 1,100 + savings 1,500 = M1 3,500; adding small time deposits 500 gives M2 4,000. Wording, four choices, key hash, feedback and money-functions-and-measures routing agree. Savings inclusion follows the [Federal Reserve H.6 definition change](https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h6/h6_technical_qa.htm).")
section(7,'Economic / Numerical Correctness',"All 793 substantive changed records were examined through checkpoint, bridge and remaining-content reviews. All revised answer sets resolve mechanically and no economically incorrect or multiply defensible revised key was found. Independent calculations used current student-visible values, not cleanup answers: 333 checkpoint calculations plus 76 additional calculations, preserved with equations, inputs, key and feedback in JSON. Numeric-free mechanism questions were reviewed for signs, constraints and short/long-run implications.\n\nCoverage includes GDP accounts and imports, value added, inventories/transfers, nominal/real GDP and deflators; labor-force flows and rates; CPI/indexation; growth/productivity; saving, debt and borrowing; reserves/capital, aggregates and quantity theory; fiscal multipliers and offsets; monetary transmission; AD-AS; Phillips expectations/sacrifice ratios; and open-economy identities/exchange rates.\n\nClass A: P52B-S4-IEA-L-001 no longer treats a lower unemployment rate alone as proof of strengthening; ECON-SP-DISTINGUISH-M1-M2-6001 preserves total initial M1 while changing composition; ECON-NL-LEGENDARYBOSS-9124 explicitly removes six unemployed people, leaving E=154, U=2, LF=156 and UR≈1.282%; P52A-CPI-LB-002 gives basket costs 100, 122, 131 and inflation 9/122≈7.377%, uniquely rounded to 7.4%; ECON-SP-FINALBOSS-4004 supplies its own adverse supply shock.\n\nGraph PG5-PC-L-006 was recomputed using visibly plotted B=(6,6), giving expected inflation 6+.6(6−5)−1.1=5.5%. There are no numerical mismatches. Correct arithmetic does not rescue a weak checkpoint or a bridge that applies another skill.")
section(8,'Advanced / Boss Verification',f"Reviewed all **42 Class-F families / 654 IDs**, using 338 normalized final task forms. All remaining numerical variants have identical normalized key, distractor and feedback wording; their arithmetic was checked per ID. {654-len(bycat['F'])} provide additional mastery evidence; {len(bycat['F'])} still only label familiar categories, repeat a channel, or perform routine arithmetic. Section 25 lists each ID with a specific reason and surgical recommendation.\n\nThe exact context ledger contains 73 total targets: 25 context-removal representatives and 48 differentiated variants, not 73 separate representatives plus 48 more. Current edits are present. Among those targets, ECON-EC-FINALBOSS-19010 and ECON-NL-MEDIUMBOSS-3015 still amount to familiar capital/technology classification. Changed wording alone does not verify added mastery evidence.")
section(9,'Repair → Bridge Verification',f"Reviewed all 84 bridges with resolved runtime repair maps and current repair text. {84-len(bycat['G'])} supply an appropriate bounded application; {len(bycat['G'])} fail because they repeat the repaired operation/conclusion or switch skill. JSON records all bridge IDs, associated repair IDs/text and routing skills. For 43139, 43160 and PMOE-NER-BR-001, concept-level support supplies the associated repair rather than a same-key map; these associations were examined explicitly.\n\nECON-NL-INVENTORY-INVESTMENT-5011 now correctly teaches transfer versus purchase under budget-accounting-and-public-saving. ECON-NL-IMPORTS-EXPORTS-NX-6004 remains imports/NX and applies cancellation: C includes 500 imported goods + 100 domestic service, while M subtracts 500, leaving GDP contribution 100.")
section(10,'Redundancy Verification',"All seven exact Class-H IDs pass. MAA-0130 retains LG-Q-9051 as the ordinary contraction chain; LG-Q-9053 reverses a target effect to a policy amount, LG-Q-9055 introduces a countershock, LG-Q-9056 compares transmission strength, LG-Q-9059 examines timing/offset, and LG-Q-9072 adds opposing money-demand pressure. MAA-0131: LG-Q-9119's indexed-loan treatment differs substantively from LG-Q-3011's inflation/real-return comparison. This was limited to the seven requested IDs.")
section(11,'Difficulty Verification',f"Reviewed all 715 Class-D final tasks. **{715-len(dissues)} coherent; {len(dissues)} mismatches.** The exceptions include three Easy labels on applications/calculations and several Hard labels on direct classification or arithmetic. Hard was accepted for genuine rule selection, conditional implication or linked steps; long wording and old ID prefixes were not used as evidence.\n\nAll 588 claimed ordinary storage moves exist and agree mechanically with their final canonical labels. This does not certify those labels pedagogically. Four of the 56 retained records still have inappropriate Hard labels. No evidence shows promotion to manufacture mode availability.")
section(12,'Mode Inventory Review',"Freshly rebuilt all 89 concept/preset inventories from before and after banks, distinguishing identical names by selection kind. Counts exactly match the cleanup ledger: **0 discrepancies; 93 newly unavailable selection/mode combinations across 41 selections; all 10 full-Macro modes pass.**\n\nEvery pool departure remains canonical and is accounted for by a storage move, specialist routing, or canonicalDifficulty remapping from an unchanged calculation/integration pool. No dropped ID, false preset membership or newly missing publication explains a shortage. Per-question destination-tier exceptions are separately recorded; their independently recommended tiers still do not justify returning them to the old demanding pool. Thus the shortages themselves qualify as **DOCUMENTED NONBLOCKING CONSEQUENCE OF HONEST CALIBRATION**. Do not raise tiers to restore them. JSON provides one entry for each of the 93 combinations, before/after counts and contributing departures.")
section(13,'Checkpoint Stage-Contract Review',"The coupling is real: composer-core.js lines 835–845 validate easyBoss→easy, mediumBoss→medium, finalBoss→hard and legendaryBoss→legendary; composition also selects canonical difficulty for mixed calculation/integration pools, with separate challengeStage handling for challenge supplements. The active checkpoint/remediation and Legendary/final-checkpoint runners pass. Checkpoint roles and stage selection remain operational, and the cleanup stores separate task-demand assessments for 597 checkpoint records.\n\nThat separate ledger is not proof of demand: for example, 43088 is called Hard there but asks only 200+20+40. Therefore EX-3 is a documented architectural limitation, but **cannot be accepted as a blanket nonblocking exception** while the 19 exact weak checkpoints remain. No engine redesign is recommended or performed.")
section(14,'Answer-Choice Verification',"All 12 Class-B targets, 11 Class-E targets and changed substantive answer sets were reviewed for distinctness, completeness, comparative length/qualification and economic plausibility. No unresolved wrong key, revised multiple-answer ambiguity or demonstrated answer-position/qualification cue was found.\n\nThe nine EX-4 records were inspected individually and in the PDF: "+', '.join(DATA['nonblockingLimitations']['EX4'])+". Their conditional clauses express the tested limitation (reserves versus lending, productivity versus total output, policy response versus curve shift, or short-run versus long-run inference); distractors remain substantive. **REVIEWED EDITORIAL SIGNAL — NONBLOCKING.** A valid conditional answer set does not certify associated skill metadata.")
section(15,'Metadata / Routing',f"Reviewed all 1,153 Class-C targets; four exceptions are in that scope and one additional stale skill was discovered while directly verifying a Class-F rewrite. One targeted stage-prefixed type remains: ECON-SP-LEGENDARY-9000 has legendary_synthesis (MAA-0125). Four directly reviewed rewrites have stale primary/repair skills: LG-Q-9111, LG-Q-2011, LG-Q-9113 and PM2C1-FED-MB-003. These are precise verification exceptions, not a request for a broader metadata rewrite. Other targeted role-only/stage-prefixed type replacements use content-operation vocabulary. Historical sourceType/sourcePool provenance is not treated as an active type defect.\n\nAll 508 MAA-0126 commonError entries now identify a concrete wrong inference, rule, direction or account. None is empty or retains the original generic template family. Shared sentence frames quote item-specific erroneous conclusions and are not generic placeholders.\n\nAll six required primary-concept and placement changes pass: "+'; '.join(f'{id} → {c}' for id,c in routes.items())+". Macro membership remains intact. The pedagogical route/skill failures described in sections 9 and 25 remain blocking despite mechanical reference validity.")
section(16,'Feedback',"All 29 Class-I targets and feedback changed with substantive rewrites were reviewed. Feedback uses current values and explains the resolved key; no empty feedback exists bank-wide. No stale scenario, truncation, option-letter dependence, wrong money-supply direction or missing opposing mechanism was found in scope. Sacrifice ratios and instructor-approved total AD offsets recompute correctly. Feedback may be correct while the paired task remains pedagogically insufficient.")
section(17,'Image / Accessibility',f"All 14 MAA-0127 records use their exact registered runtimePath; source files exist and publication/PDF embed the correct assets. imageAlt, graphDescription and graphRequired were checked against the visual graphs. Descriptions identify axes, curves and labeled points without giving the answer. All 14 were included in visual PDF inspection. **{len(assetHashes)} graph-asset baseline hashes remain identical**; no graph geometry defect is asserted or invented.")
section(18,'Shared General / Micro Regression Check',"Compared the complete canonical record and every placement for all **6,623 IDs** in the pre-Macro General/Micro union. **0 differences**, including stem, alternatives, key hash, feedback, difficulty, metadata, skill and routing. Exact area counts and membership remain General 1,589 and Micro 6,301.\n\nConsulted general_economics_final_verification.md and general_economics_exception_closure.md (25 scoped exceptions closed), plus microeconomics_final_verification.md and microeconomics_exception_closure.md (three exact closures). The approved pre-Macro commit includes those completed closures; comparison is against that state rather than an earlier pre-closure bank. Old reports and evidence were preserved.")
section(19,'Publication Limitations',"EX-1 confirmed independently: ECON-SP-MAP-AD-AS-TO-PC-5061 and ECON-SP-MAP-AD-AS-TO-PC-6052 were absent from student publication both before and after cleanup. Both remain canonical and occur in faculty CSV/PDF. No new omission exists. **PRE-EXISTING NONBLOCKING LIMITATION.**")
section(20,'Validation / Build Results',"**29/29 current active Composer runners pass; 14/14 exporter tests pass.** Coverage includes canonical integrity, scope, outcomes, graph sync, question quality, lineage, checkpoint/remediation, Legendary/final checkpoint, mode availability, Trial by Graph and student build. Inline JavaScript compiles. No test or expectation was changed by verification. A temporary write-only preload redirected fixed-path generated test evidence into tmp to preserve prior cleanup artifacts; all fixture reads and assertions remained unchanged. Logs are retained in the new verification evidence directory. Passing structural tests did not override the independent semantic findings.")
section(21,'Student Publication',"Fresh Macro publication contains **4,743 unique IDs from 4,745 canonical Macro IDs**, with exactly the two verified old omissions. Published canonical content/answer parity has zero mismatches, all answer hashes resolve, all 14 repaired graph paths embed, all 10 supported full-Macro modes validate, and every inline script compiles. No publication failure is hidden by the documented omissions.")
section(22,'CSV Fidelity',"Normal exporter regeneration completed without manual export edits. Macro CSV has **4,745 rows / 4,745 unique IDs / 169 columns**. All fields were compared with freshly derived canonical exporter records, including source and routing metadata, options, answer index/letter/text, feedback, difficulty, type and images: **0 mismatches**. General and Micro companion CSVs likewise have zero all-field mismatches.")
section(23,'PDF Fidelity',f"Macro PDF has **{EXP['pdf_pages']} pages**, all 4,745 IDs once in expected order, {EXP['images']} embedded images, {EXP['pdf_links']} links and {EXP['pdf_outline_entries']} outline entries. Full text/content verification finds complete stems, alternatives, keys and feedback; zero blank content pages, replacement characters, bounds errors, missing required images, link errors, split question cores or page-render failures. Every page rendered.\n\nVisually inspected **49 selected pages on 25 contact sheets**, covering all required adjudications, representative checkpoints/bridges, all 14 accessibility targets and all nine EX-4 signals. No clipping or legibility defect was found. In 43 cases header/metadata remains on the preceding page while the entire question core starts on the next page; this is disclosed as pagination whitespace, not a split core or lost content. Exact page manifests and PDF hash are in JSON.")
section(24,'Repository Scope',"The pre-cleanup comparison shows only canonical/derived library data, approved taxonomy/registry/outcome changes, cleanup tooling/evidence, approved-state validation adapters and regenerated exports. Twelve tracked content diffs are confined to four data files and eight validation adapters/contracts. Existing cleanup helper and expectation files are accounted for. No adaptive engine, telemetry, polished-game content, UI logic or unrelated graph bytes changed.\n\nVerification itself left **14,867 protected files byte-identical**. That protection includes current source, tests, prior audit/cleanup reports and existing evidence. Writes are limited to these new reports/evidence, temporary verification artifacts, interpreter caches and normal regenerated exports. The before/after protected-file manifest and source hash are preserved with this report.")
section(25,'Remaining Exceptions',table(['Exception','Question ID / Selection','Original finding','Problem','Evidence','Severity','Blocking?','Recommended surgical action'],[(e['exceptionID'],e['questionID'],', '.join(e['originalFindings']) or 'Direct changed-record verification',e['problem'],e['evidence'],e['severity'],'Yes',e['recommendedSurgicalAction']) for e in exceptions])+"\n\nThese recommendations were not implemented. EX-1, EX-2 and EX-4 are nonblocking as verified above. EX-3 describes real architecture but does not excuse the listed checkpoint failures. Findings are content judgments under the supplied calibration, not claims that an unadministered item has empirically measured student difficulty.")
